    "seo_question": "What supplication did Gabriel teach Ya'qub to restore his sight in the story of Yusuf?",
    "summary": "This lengthy narrative from al-Amali al-Saduq, narrated through Ibn Abbas, retells the Quranic story of Prophet Yusuf (AS) and his brothers in expanded detail. It covers multiple visits to Egypt, the detention of Sham'un, the sending of Binyamin, the incident of the king's measuring cup, and Yusuf's self-revelation. A distinctive Shia element appears when Gabriel teaches Ya'qub a supplication invoking Muhammad, Ali, Fatima, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn, which immediately restores his sight. The hadith also includes a report from Imam al-Sadiq about Yusuf's punishment for not dismounting for his father.",
